  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        518.4614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Yellowstone's iconic grey wolves had been exterminated by 1926. On 12 January 1995 eight wolves captured in Alberta, Canada, were hauled to the park in crates; six more followed. Released from enclosures in late March, they roamed the wilderness."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        430.7614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.9614173228347
      ],
      "text": "In February 2014 a viral video narrated by writer George Monbiot spun a compelling narrative: elk, thinned by wolves and wary of them, retreated from valleys, letting willows flourish and riverbanks stabilise. Ecologists call this a trophic cascade: predators eat or deter plant-eaters, and vegetation rebounds."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        323.2614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        422.2614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Yet the census undermined the thinning claim: elk on the park's northern range peaked at about 19,000 in January 1994 and were dwindling before wolves arrived, depleted by hunters, drought, and bears. Fear looked weak too: in June 2013 Arthur Middleton's University of Wyoming team found that collared elk east of the park kept grazing unless wolves ventured within half a mile."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        195.96141732283468,
        461.8976377952756,
        314.7614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Trees fared no better: in November 2021 Utah State University's Elaine Brice showed that sampling only the tallest aspens overstated regrowth four- to sevenfold. The deeper flaw was water. Colorado State University's Tom Hobbs and David Cooper had excluded elk with fences and built artificial beaver dams. In January 2024 they reported: eroding streams had cut so deep that stunted willows no longer reached water."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        88.46141732283468,
        461.8976377952756,
        187.46141732283468
      ],
      "text": "In January 2025 Oregon State University's William Ripple, an advocate of the hypothesis, reported one of the world's strongest cascades; critics disputed his methods. The question is unresolved, but the wolves' shadow looks fainter than the fable suggested, and the science messier. A discipline willing to revise its cherished example may deserve more trust than the fable ever did."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        537.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "黄石公园那些标志性的灰狼，到1926年已遭赶尽杀绝。1995年1月12日，八只在加拿大艾伯塔省捕获的狼装在板条箱里，一路拖运进了公园；随后又来了六只。3月下旬，它们被放出围栏，得以在荒野中四处游荡。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        449.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        529.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "2014年2月，一段火了的视频，由作家乔治·蒙比奥特解说，编织出一个引人入胜的故事。片中说，麋鹿被狼捕杀得数量变少，又处处提防着狼，便撤离了河谷，这让柳树繁茂起来，河岸也稳固下来。生态学家把这称为营养级联：捕食者吃掉或吓阻食草动物，然后植被得以恢复生长。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        340.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        440.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "然而，普查结果首先就动摇了鹿被狼吃少了这一说法。黄石北部草场的麋鹿在1994年1月达到约19,000头的峰值，狼还没来就已日渐减少；鹿群被猎人、干旱和熊不断地消耗着。恐惧一说看来也站不住。2013年6月，阿瑟·米德尔顿领导的怀俄明大学团队发现，园区东侧戴项圈的麋鹿照样吃草，除非狼胆敢踏入进半英里以内。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        232.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        332.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "树木方面的证据也好不到哪里去：2021年11月，犹他州立大学的伊莱恩·布赖斯指出，只抽样测量最高的山杨，会把它们的再生程度夸大四到七倍。更根本的缺陷出在水上。科罗拉多州立大学的汤姆·霍布斯和戴维·库珀用围栏把麋鹿挡在外面，并修建人工海狸坝。2024年1月，他们报告说，不断冲蚀河床的溪流下切太深，那些矮小的柳树已经够不着水了。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        123.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        223.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "2025年1月，这一假说的倡导者、俄勒冈州立大学的威廉·里普尔发文称，黄石的级联效应位居世界最强之列；批评者则对他的方法提出质疑。问题仍悬而未决，但狼投下的影子比谣传所暗示的更加无力，相关研究也要复杂纠结得多。一门学科如果愿意去修正（甚至推翻）自己最珍视的完美案例，那么这门学科，比那个完美的谣传本身更值得信任。"
    }
  ],
